    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Reuleaux Triangle" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="46.75" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="A circle is not the only shape with the same width in every direction. This one is made of three 60° arcs, each centered at the opposite corner.\n\nRoll it between two parallel lines and they never move apart. That is why it can drill (almost) square holes. Some coins are shapes of constant width too, like the British 50p, with seven sides: a machine measuring across them gets the same answer every way." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="94.75" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
